 34NA c  2014Do05: A 345-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam was accelerated by the
 34NA2c  superconducting ring cyclotron (SRC) at RIKEN. A 236-MeV/nucleon       
 34NA3c  {+36}Mg secondary beam was produced by the fragmentation of {+48}Ca on 
 34NA4c  a Be target and separated by the BigRIPS separator using the           
 34NA5c  B|r-|DE-B|r method. The secondary reaction targets were 2.54-g/cm{+2}  
 34NA6c  thick carbon and 2.13-g/cm{+2} thick CH{-2} polyethylene. The secondary
 34NA7c  reaction products {+33}Na, {+34}Na, and {+35}Na were identified by the magnetic spectrometer         
 34NA8c  ZeroDegree using the B|r-|DE-ToF method. |g rays in coincidence with   
 34NA9c  {+34}Na were detected using the DALI2 array of 186 large NaI(Tl)       
 34NAAc  detectors. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g, and              
 34NABc  ({+34}Na)|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |p, and bands. Compared with    
 34NACc  shell-model calculations using the SPDF-M effective interaction.       
 35NA cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies.                         
 35NA cL J$From shell-model calculations.                                       
 35NA cL BAND(A)$K|p=(3/2+) rotational band predicted by the shell model.       
 34NA c  2014Do05: E=236 MeV/nucleon {+36}Mg beam produced by fragmentation of  
 34NA2c  345 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam on a {+9}Be target at the         
 34NA3c  RIBF-RIKEN facility. The {+36}Mg was separated by BigRIPS fragment     
 34NA4c  separator using B|r-|DE-B|r method. The secondary reaction targets were
 34NA5c  2.54 g/cm{+2} thick carbon and 2.13 g/cm{+2} thick CH{-2} polyethylene.
 34NA6c  Gamma rays were detected using DALI2 array of 186 large NaI(Tl)        
 34NA7c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin. Deduced level in {+34}Na.     
